            "text": "<h2>A Family Tradition</h2><p><strong>Introduction</strong><br/><br/>Champagne Guerlet-Deguerne is a small, family-run Champagne producer based in the village of <strong>Chamery</strong>, located in the heart of the <strong>Montagne de Reims</strong> region. The estate has been family-owned for over six generations and is now led by the children of Patrice Guerlet and Véronique Deguerne, who are gradually taking over with a fresh and environmentally conscious vision.</p><p><strong>Location and Terroir</strong><br/><br/>Chamery lies within the Montagne de Reims, an area known for its rolling hills and diverse soils, particularly <strong>clay-limestone terroir</strong> that supports all three major Champagne grape varieties. Guerlet-Deguerne's vineyards reflect this diversity, and the family’s deep knowledge of the land allows them to craft wines with precision and character.</p><p><strong>Champagnes Offered</strong><br/><br/>Guerlet-Deguerne produces a thoughtful range of Champagnes that highlight the expression of their terroir and blend heritage with modernity.</p><p><strong>Non-Vintage Champagnes</strong><br/><br/>Their core cuvées typically feature blends of <strong>Pinot Noir, Pinot Meunier, and Chardonnay</strong>, vinified with care and aged extensively—often over 30 months—to bring balance and depth to the wines. Partial malolactic fermentation and stainless-steel vinification preserve freshness and purity.</p><p><strong>Rosé and Blanc de Blancs</strong><br/><br/>The house also produces a <strong>Brut Rosé d’assemblage</strong> that is vibrant and fruit-driven, as well as a <strong>Blanc de Blancs</strong> that emphasizes finesse, freshness, and fine mineral structure from their Chardonnay parcels.</p><p><strong>Special Cuvées</strong><br/><br/>Small-production still wines (Coteaux Champenois) and single-variety expressions—such as their 100% Meunier “Les Meuniers de Chamery”—showcase the estate’s willingness to explore and push boundaries while staying true to its roots.</p><p><strong>Winemaking Techniques</strong><br/><br/>The estate combines traditional methods with a commitment to sustainability. Guerlet-Deguerne became <strong>certified organic in 2023</strong>, a reflection of their work with cover crops, reduced chemical use, and soil health practices. Vinification occurs in stainless steel, oak barrels, or a combination, depending on the cuvée.</p><p><strong>Conclusion</strong><br/><br/>Champagne Guerlet-Deguerne is an exciting and authentic grower-producer, known for its <strong>family heritage, terroir-driven wines, and strong commitment to sustainability</strong>. With an increasing focus on precision and low-intervention viticulture, the estate is earning recognition for both its classic cuvées and innovative releases.</p>",
